@baseUrl = https://localhost:7179
@adminEmail = admin@flyreservation.local
# Type your AdminUser:Password (user secrets) here while testing. Do not commit it
@adminPassword = CHANGE_ME
# A throwaway customer for development, not a secret. Register it once with CUSTOMER-1
@customerEmail = alice@test.com
@customerPassword = alice-password-123

### AUTH) Login as admin. Send this first: the admin requests below read the token from its response
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}


### CUSTOMER-1) Register the customer once (409 from the second time on)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{customerEmail}}",
  "password": "{{customerPassword}}"
}

### CUSTOMER-2) Login as the customer. The customer requests below read the token from its response
# @name customer
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{customerEmail}}",
  "password": "{{customerPassword}}"
}

### 1) List all reservations (admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 1b) My reservations, newest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 2) Create reservation. passengerId must be one of mine (Passengers.http 1b), otherwise 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "flightId": 3,
  "passengerId": 3
}

### 7) Deney 17-E: same key twice → same PNR (click Send twice)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: deney-17-1

{
  "flightId": 2,
  "passengerId": 4
}

### 3) Get reservation by id
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations/2
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 4) Cancel reservation
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations/6
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 5) Deney B2: try to set server-side fields from client (DTO should ignore them)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "flightId": 1,
  "passengerId": 1,
  "pnrCode": "HACK01",
  "createdAt": "2000-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "id": 999
}

### 6) Deney B3: reservation for a non-existent flight
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "flightId": 9999,
  "passengerId": 1
}

### Pay a reservation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/reservations/1/payment
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.$.accessToken}}
